{"gold":[{"independent_answer":"620","question_sha256":"74e22047aee0787e9ccb1d21390f9eef15fd75b77ff2df7d48b962cc52a867bf","reason":"Eight hours split equally gives 4 hours at each speed. The distances are 70×4=280 and 85×4=340 kilometers, so the total is 280+340=620, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-6777"},{"independent_answer":"15","question_sha256":"936fdf13b8fe50a31b813246f28bae985ed4e5e87e6d8fe35fea533d0257e334","reason":"Four hours is 240 minutes. Two essays take 2×60=120 minutes and five paragraphs take 5×15=75, leaving 240−195=45 minutes. At 3 minutes each, 45÷3=15 questions, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-3299"},{"independent_answer":"448","question_sha256":"54cd56bf0e3f5267a767ad45a62a4d739b5844448f56bf31b187560559ee01a1","reason":"The first craft travels 448 miles in 0.5 hour, giving 896 mph. The second arrives at 4:00 pm and therefore travels for 1 hour, giving 448 mph. Their speed difference is 896−448=448 mph, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-1231"},{"independent_answer":"128","question_sha256":"989c3a0d3ba37c410f4d88557e6fcd4b18eef81f31668359a071674fa359d6ed","reason":"One sixth of 24 hours is 4 hours, divided equally into 4/3 hours per reading type. The pages are 21×4/3=28, 30×4/3=40, and 45×4/3=60; their sum is 128, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-1530"},{"independent_answer":"120","question_sha256":"63aca387e2aea28d4f114f6a467b8372fd07d91e98fc931fec41762685562eee","reason":"Two hours is 120 minutes, so 20×120=2400 drops are delivered. At 5 ml per 100 drops, this is 2400÷100×5=120 ml, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-6925"},{"independent_answer":"202","question_sha256":"aea723e4b4fa2217846054ebaaf8e4dc9079c0592ed06d08a75d41579e1355ca","reason":"Hourly pay is 9×8=72 dollars. The additional earnings are 15×7=105, 10×2=20, and 1×5=5 dollars. Thus total earnings are 72+105+20+5=202 dollars, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-6985"},{"independent_answer":"720","question_sha256":"c9a37a130b4019a4a572948ca13dffb86627a058cd07b3a89febdab29bec6abb","reason":"Jake earns 3×6=18 dollars per hour and works 5×8=40 hours. His earnings are 18×40=720 dollars, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-7012"},{"independent_answer":"16","question_sha256":"051ca197064381cdd99fe1b08b67e9dc3936c61b61e0942328d12573fea8baca","reason":"Ten 8-hour shifts provide 10×8=80 work hours. At 5 hours per chair, Ben completes 80÷5=16 chairs, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-899"}],"reviews":[{"checkable_expectation":true,"evidence_spans":["The first half of the trip is 4 hours (8 / 2)","70 km/h × 4 h = 280 km","280 km + 340 km = 620 km"],"first_person":false,"full_text_read":true,"grounded_operations":true,"key":"gsm8k-train-6777:rich","neutral_prefix_compatible":true,"no_padding":true,"prefix_reason":"Every claim follows from the question and displayed arithmetic; the target claims no external feedback or hidden event. However, it contains no substantive first-person account of performing the operations.","raw_call_sha256":"3e226e376d70901ca13f1cabefbe5f675f2b82ee20ae64b5b5094c620101e4fc","reason":"The time split, distance products, and sum are correct and supply checkable, reusable reasoning without filler. The response is nevertheless entirely impersonal, so first_person fails.","reusable_content":true,"status":"FAIL","student_prefix_sha256":"8fb2c179553adda647098d73b0bc40846fff51a7e45311b53c0d6f8f7c9ffbe0","target_sha256":"237f462a6aac5d445ccfbef0519f348f02a72774dcaf3d09f615776e09707284"},{"checkable_expectation":true,"evidence_spans":["I broke the trip into two halves, each lasting 4 hours.","70 km/h × 4 h = 280 km","280 km + 340 km = 620 km"],"first_person":true,"full_text_read":true,"grounded_operations":true,"key":"gsm8k-train-6777:new_record","neutral_prefix_compatible":true,"no_padding":true,"prefix_reason":"The first-person calculat